# OpenSpec SDD Workflow

Use Specification-Driven Development for every project change.

## Required Gate

Before implementation, create or update an OpenSpec change under:

```text
openspec/changes/<change-name>/
```

Required artifacts:

- `.openspec.yaml`
- `proposal.md`
- `design.md`
- `tasks.md`
- `specs/<capability>/spec.md`

If the OpenSpec CLI is unavailable, create the artifacts manually using the
existing repository structure.

## Required Skill

Use `$sdd-openspec-multiagent` before project changes.

Use the OpenSpec skills when available:

- `$openspec-explore`
- `$openspec-propose`
- `$openspec-apply-change`
- `$openspec-sync-specs`
- `$openspec-archive-change`

## Apply Rule

Do not edit product, API, UI, mobile, backend, test, deployment, security, or
infrastructure behavior unless the OpenSpec change has tasks and acceptance
criteria.

Mark tasks complete as implementation progresses.
